 \"Marlies Gohr\"","if let index = recordTimes.firstIndex(where: { $0.0 == runner }) {","    let time = recordTimes[index].1","    print(\"\\(runner) set a 100m record of \\(time) seconds.\")","} else {","    print(\"\\(runner) couldn't be found in the records.\")","}","\/\/ Prints \"Marlies Gohr set a 100m record of 10.81 seconds.\""]},{"type":"heading","text":"Key-Value Pairs as a Function Parameter","anchor":"Key-Value-Pairs-as-a-Function-Parameter","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When calling a function with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyValuePairs"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter, you can pass"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a Swift dictionary literal without causing a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Dictionary"},{"type":"text","text":" to be created."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This capability can be especially important when the order of elements in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the literal is significant."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For example, you could create an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IntPairs"},{"text":" structure that holds a list of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"two-integer tuples and use an initializer that accepts a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyValuePairs"},{"text":" instance.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct IntPairs {","    var elements: [(Int, Int)]","","    init(_ elements: KeyValuePairs<Int, Int>) {","        self.elements = Array(elements)","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you’re ready to create a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IntPairs"},{"type":"text","text":" instance, use a dictionary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"literal as the parameter to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IntPairs"},{"type":"text","text":" 